d 'TABTOOLS': module to export publication-ready descriptive, model, survival, and rate tables to Excel and Markdown
d
d  tabtools is a suite of commands that turn descriptive,
d regression, treatment-effect, survival, rate, and composite
d results into publication-ready tables written to formatted Excel
d workbooks, GitHub-Flavored Markdown, CSV files, or Stata frames.
d table1_tc and desctab build Table 1 descriptive tables with
d automatic group comparison tests, standardized differences,
d weights, and small-cell suppression; crosstab produces
d cross-tabulations with chi-square or exact tests, odds ratios,
d risk ratios, risk differences, and trend tests; regtab exports
d coefficients from most estimation commands, including
d multi-model, multi-equation, and mixed-effects layouts with model
d statistics; effecttab tabulates teffects and margins results;
d tabcell formats a single estimate, p-value, n (%), or median
d (IQR) cell; outtab reports binary outcomes by exposure with model
d ratios; stratetab and ratetab tabulate events, person-time, and
d incidence rates with confidence intervals (exact, Poisson, or
d cluster-robust in ratetab); survtab reports Kaplan-Meier
d survival, restricted mean survival, and median survival; comptab
d and hrcomptab assemble vertical model composites and
d rate-interlocked tables; puttab styles any in-memory dataset,
d frame, or matrix, and stacktab assembles multi-sheet composite
d workbooks. All commands share one set of output and formatting
d options (fonts, borders, shading, digits, titles, footnotes), and
d tabtools manages persistent session defaults and destinations.
d Results are returned in r(), including the rendered table and a
d methods sentence. 
d
d KW: table 1
d KW: descriptive statistics
d KW: regression tables
d KW: publication tables
d KW: Excel
d KW: xlsx
d KW: Markdown
d KW: incidence rates
d KW: survival
d KW: Kaplan-Meier
d KW: cross-tabulation
d KW: small-cell suppression
d
d Requires: Stata version 17
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d Support: email timothy.copeland@@ki.se
d
